    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d441">

                <pb facs="0769" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg699"/>

                <head>No. 440.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Cayetano
                            Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-10-24"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 24,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to the Department’s note to you
                    of the 15th ultimo, I have now the honor to inclose to you, for the information
                    of the Government of Mexico, copy of a letter from the Secretary of War of the
                    19th instant, covering a report from General Crook, stating that it would be
                    difficult, if not wholly impracticable, to carry out the suggestions presented
                    in your note of August 16 last relative to the return of articles stolen from
                    Mexican citizens by the Indians recently captured by that officer.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d441-a1.xml" xpointer="d441-a1"/>
